==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|cōnstituēns}}, present participle of {{m|la|cōnstituō|t=I establish}}, from {{m|la|com-|t=together}} + {{m|la|statuo|t=I set, place, establish}}; see [[statute]] or [[statue]], and compare [[institute]] and [[restitute]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-uk-constituent.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# being a [[part]], or [[component]] of a [[whole]]
#* Dryden
#*: Body, soul, and reason are the three parts necessarily '''constituent''' of a man.
# [[authorized]] to make a [[constitution]]
#* Junius
#*: A question of right arises between the '''constituent''' and representative body.

